{% comment %}
  ============================================================================
  MIL-STD-2073 CODE LOOKUP
  Royco Packaging, Inc.  —  sections/mil-std-2073-decoder.liquid

  WHAT THIS IS
    A self-contained Shopify theme section that decodes MIL-STD-2073-1E
    (w/CHANGE 4) Appendix J packaging codes. One lookup box per Appendix J
    table. Results give the full requirement, not just the table line, and
    hyperlink every referenced specification to the matching Royco
    collection or product.

  INSTALL
    1. Shopify admin > Online Store > Themes > ... > Edit code
    2. Sections > Add a new section > name it  mil-std-2073-decoder
    3. Replace the generated contents with this entire file, Save
    4. Open the page you want it on in the Theme Editor > Add section >
       "MIL-STD-2073 Code Lookup"

  TEXT SIZE
    Theme Editor > Appearance > "Base text size". Everything in the section
    scales from that one number.

  MAINTAINING THE PRODUCT LINKS
    Search this file for  specLinks:  (near the top of the <script> block).
    That object maps a specification designator to a collection handle.
    Change a handle there and every link that mentions that spec updates
    everywhere in the tool. A handle left blank ("") renders as plain text
    rather than a link that 404s.

  SOURCE
    MIL-STD-2073-1E w/CHANGE 4. Code tables from Appendix J, Tables J-I
    through J-X. Method of preservation detail from section 5.2.3.
  ============================================================================
{% endcomment %}

<div
  class="royco-2073"
  id="royco-2073-{{ section.id }}"
  data-collection-root="{{ section.settings.collection_root | escape }}"
  data-product-root="{{ section.settings.product_root | escape }}"
>
  <div class="royco-2073__inner">

    {% if section.settings.heading != blank %}
      <h1 class="royco-2073__heading">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h1>
    {% endif %}

    {% if section.settings.intro != blank %}
      <div class="royco-2073__intro rte">{{ section.settings.intro }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="royco-2073__grid" data-role="field-grid"></div>

    {% if section.settings.disclaimer != blank %}
      <div class="royco-2073__disclaimer rte">{{ section.settings.disclaimer }}</div>
    {% endif %}

  </div>
</div>

{% style %}
  #royco-2073-{{ section.id }} {
    --rc-ink:    {{ section.settings.color_ink }};
    --rc-muted:  {{ section.settings.color_muted }};
    --rc-accent: {{ section.settings.color_accent }};
    --rc-bg:     {{ section.settings.color_bg }};
    --rc-panel:  {{ section.settings.color_panel }};
    --rc-line:   {{ section.settings.color_line }};
    --rc-radius: 10px;
    /* Every size in the section is derived from this one number, set in
       Theme Editor > Appearance > Base text size. */
    --rc-fs:     {{ section.settings.text_size }}px;
  }
  #royco-2073-{{ section.id }} {
    background: var(--rc-bg);
    color: var(--rc-ink);
    padding: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px 1.25rem {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    font-size: var(--rc-fs);
  }
{% endstyle %}

<style>
  .royco-2073 *, .royco-2073 *::before, .royco-2073 *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
  .royco-2073__inner { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; }

  .royco-2073__heading {
    margin: 0 0 .5em;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * 2);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .royco-2073__intro {
    margin: 0 0 2em;
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * 1.06);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--rc-muted);
  }
  .royco-2073__intro p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* ---- card grid ---- */
  .royco-2073__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(26rem, 1fr));
    align-items: start;
  }
  .royco-2073__card {
    border: 1px solid var(--rc-line);
    border-radius: var(--rc-radius);
    background: var(--rc-panel);
    padding: 1.15rem 1.2rem 1.2rem;
  }
  .royco-2073__cardhead {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between;
    gap: .6rem; margin-bottom: .7em;
  }
  .royco-2073__cardtitle {
    margin: 0; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.25;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * 1.12);
  }
  .royco-2073__tablabel {
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * .78);
    color: var(--rc-muted); letter-spacing: .07em;
    text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .royco-2073__input {
    display: block; width: 100%;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * 1.25);
    letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rc-ink); background: var(--rc-bg);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--rc-line); border-radius: 8px;
    padding: .55em .6em;
  }
  .royco-2073__input::placeholder {
    letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none;
    font-family: inherit; font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * .8); color: var(--rc-muted);
  }
  .royco-2073__input:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--rc-accent); outline-offset: 1px; border-color: var(--rc-accent);
  }

  /* ---- result ---- */
  .royco-2073__cardres {
    margin-top: .8em;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * 1);
    line-height: 1.62;
  }
  .royco-2073__cardres a {
    color: var(--rc-accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .royco-2073__cardres--err { color: #b3352a; }
  .royco-2073__cardres--idle { color: var(--rc-muted); font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * .9); }

  /* The table line reads as the headline; 5.2.3 detail follows as prose. */
  .royco-2073__lead { font-weight: 650; }
  .royco-2073__detail { margin-top: .45em; display: block; }

  /* ---- long procedural text: clamped, never truncated ---- */
  .royco-2073__longinner { position: relative; max-height: 11em; overflow: hidden; }
  .royco-2073__longinner::after {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; height: 2.4em;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, var(--rc-panel));
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .royco-2073__long.is-open .royco-2073__longinner { max-height: none; }
  .royco-2073__long.is-open .royco-2073__longinner::after { display: none; }
  .royco-2073__more {
    margin-top: .5em; font-family: inherit; font-weight: 650;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * .92);
    color: var(--rc-accent); background: none; border: 0; padding: 0;
    cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .royco-2073__more::after { content: " ▾"; text-decoration: none; }
  .royco-2073__long.is-open .royco-2073__more::after { content: " ▴"; }

  /* ---- Royco products ---- */
  .royco-2073__stock {
    display: block; margin-top: .75em; padding-top: .65em;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--rc-line);
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * .94); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .royco-2073__stock strong { color: var(--rc-ink); font-weight: 650; }
  .royco-2073__stock a { display: inline-block; margin: .15em .55em .15em 0; }

  /* ---- browse ---- */
  .royco-2073__browse {
    margin-top: .8em; font-family: inherit;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * .92);
    color: var(--rc-muted); background: none; border: 0; padding: 0;
    cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .royco-2073__browse:hover { color: var(--rc-ink); }
  .royco-2073__list {
    margin-top: .7em; max-height: 20rem; overflow-y: auto;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rc-line);
  }
  .royco-2073__listitem {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3.5rem 1fr; gap: .6rem;
    width: 100%; text-align: left; font-family: inherit;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * .92); line-height: 1.5;
    background: none; border: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rc-line);
    padding: .55em .3em; cursor: pointer; color: inherit;
  }
  .royco-2073__listitem:hover { background: var(--rc-bg); }
  .royco-2073__listitem code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-weight: 650; color: var(--rc-accent);
  }
  .royco-2073__listitem span { color: var(--rc-muted); }

  .royco-2073__disclaimer {
    margin-top: 2em; max-width: 78ch;
    font-size: calc(var(--rc-fs) * .82); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--rc-muted);
  }
  .royco-2073__disclaimer p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .royco-2073__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>

{% raw %}
<script>
(function () {
  "use strict";

  /* == DATA ================================================================ */
  /* ============================================================
     MIL-STD-2073-1E w/CHANGE 4 — Appendix J code tables
     Data block. Kept separate during authoring, inlined into the
     Shopify section at build time.
     ============================================================ */
  var MS2073 = {

  /* ---- Spec designator -> Royco collection handle -------------
     VERIFIED against roycopackaging.com/collections.json.
     Every handle below is a live collection on the store.
     An empty string means "Royco has no collection for this spec yet" —
     the designator renders as plain text, not a broken link. Create the
     collection, drop its handle in here, and the links light up
     everywhere the spec is mentioned.

     Specs currently unlinked, in rough order of how often they appear in
     Appendix J results:
       PPP-C-795 / A-A-3129 / PPP-C-1797 / A-A-1898  (cushioning)
       MIL-PRF-26514 / A-A-59136                     (foam)
       MIL-PRF-16173                                 (CP compounds)
       MIL-STD-129                                   (labels)
       A-A-203 / MIL-P-130 / QQ-A-1876 / A-A-3174    (wraps, foil, poly)
       ASTM D4727 / ASTM D5168                       (other fiberboard)
     ------------------------------------------------------------ */
  specLinks: {
    "MIL-DTL-117":           "in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags",
    "MIL-PRF-131":           "mil-prf-131",
    "MIL-PRF-121":           "mil-prf-121",
    "MIL-PRF-81705":         "mil-prf-81705",
    "MIL-PRF-22191":         "mil-prf-22191",
    "MIL-PRF-3420":          "mil-prf-3420",
    "MIL-DTL-17667":         "mil-dtl-17667",
    "MIL-D-3464":            "mil-d-3464",
    "MIL-DTL-22020":         "corrosion-protection",
    "MIL-PRF-22019":         "corrosion-protection",
    "MIL-DTL-6060":          "in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags",
    "MIL-DTL-81997":         "static-control-materials",
    "ASTM D5486":            "mil-spec-tapes",
    "ASTM D5118/D5118M":     "astm-d5118-v3c-and-w5c-boxes",
    "ASTM D5118":            "astm-d5118-v3c-and-w5c-boxes",

    "MIL-PRF-26514":         "",
    "MIL-PRF-16173":         "",
    "A-A-3129":              "",
    "PPP-C-795":             "",
    "PPP-C-1797":            "",
    "A-A-1898":              "",
    "A-A-59136":             "",
    "A-A-3174":              "",
    "A-A-203":               "",
    "MIL-P-130":             "",
    "QQ-A-1876":             "",
    "ASTM D4727/D4727M":     "",
    "ASTM D4727":            "",
    "ASTM D5168":            "",
    "MIL-STD-129":           ""
  },

  /* Display names for the "Royco supplies" links. A handle with no entry
     here falls back to a title-cased version of the handle itself.  */
  linkLabels: {
    "in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags":          "In-Stock Heat Seal Barrier Bags",
    "mil-prf-131":                              "MIL-PRF-131 Barrier Material",
    "mil-prf-121":                              "MIL-PRF-121",
    "mil-prf-81705":                            "MIL-PRF-81705",
    "mil-prf-22191":                            "MIL-PRF-22191",
    "mil-prf-3420":                             "MIL-PRF-3420 VCI Wrapping",
    "mil-dtl-17667":                            "MIL-DTL-17667 Wrapping Paper",
    "mil-d-3464":                               "MIL-D-3464 Desiccant",
    "desiccants":                               "Desiccants & Moisture Control",
    "bulk-desiccant":                           "Bulk Desiccant",
    "capsules-cannisters":                      "Capsules & Cannisters",
    "static-control-materials":                 "ESD Protection",
    "corrosion-protection":                     "Volatile Corrosion Inhibitors",
    "grease-water-vapor-proof-barrier-materials":"Roll Stock & Barrier Materials",
    "astm-d5118-v3c-and-w5c-boxes":             "ASTM D5118 V3c & W5c Boxes",
    "mil-spec-tapes":                           "ASTM D5486 Packaging Tape",
    "tapes":                                    "MIL-SPEC Packaging Tapes",
    "wax-wraps":                                "Industrial Wax & Barrier Wraps",

    "product:specpack-1e1-foil-watervaporproof-barrier-bags": "SpecPack 1E1 — Foil Watervaporproof Bags",
    "product:specpack-2-c-1-greaseproof-barrier-bags":        "SpecPack 2C1 — Medium Duty Greaseproof Bags",
    "product:specpack-light-duty-greaseproof-barrier-bags":   "SpecPack 3C1 — Light Duty Greaseproof Bags",
    "product:specpack-1f1":                                   "SpecPack 1F1 — ESD Watervaporproof Bags",
    "product:static-shield-bags":                             "Commercial Static Shield Bags"
  },

  /* Extra links attached to specific codes where the descriptive text
     names no stocked specification, or where Royco has an exact product
     match for the code. Prefix a handle with "product:" to link a single
     product instead of a collection.

     The SpecPack entries below are exact matches: a J-VII container code
     is a MIL-DTL-117 Type/Class/Style combination, and SpecPack part
     numbers use that same Type/Class/Style scheme. B9 really is 1F1.   */
  extraLinks: {
    "J-I":   { "50": ["desiccants","mil-d-3464"],
               "51": ["desiccants","in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags"],
               "52": ["desiccants","in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags"],
               "53": ["desiccants","in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags"],
               "54": ["desiccants"],
               "55": ["desiccants"],
               "31": ["in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags"],
               "32": ["in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags"],
               "33": ["in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags","mil-prf-121"],
               "41": ["in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags","mil-prf-131"],
               "42": ["in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags","mil-prf-131"],
               "43": ["in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags","mil-prf-131"] },
    "J-Ia":  { "DW": ["desiccants","mil-prf-131"],
               "GX": ["product:specpack-1f1","static-control-materials"],
               "GS": ["corrosion-protection"] },
    "J-IV":  { "K3": ["mil-prf-81705","static-control-materials"],
               "MB": ["mil-prf-3420"] },
    "J-VII": { "BS": ["product:specpack-1e1-foil-watervaporproof-barrier-bags"],
               "BE": ["product:specpack-2-c-1-greaseproof-barrier-bags"],
               "BV": ["product:specpack-light-duty-greaseproof-barrier-bags"],
               "B9": ["product:specpack-1f1"],
               "BT": ["corrosion-protection"],
               "SH": ["in-stock-heat-seal-barrier-bags"] }
  },

  /* ---- Field definitions, in packaging-code sequence ---------- */
  fields: [
    { key:"J-I",    pos:[1,2],   len:2, label:"Method of Preservation",        table:"J-I",    also:"J-Ia", ref:"J.4.2" },
    { key:"J-II",   pos:[3,3],   len:1, label:"Cleaning Procedure",            table:"J-II",   ref:"J.4.4" },
    { key:"J-III",  pos:[4,5],   len:2, label:"Preservative Material",         table:"J-III",  ref:"J.4.5" },
    { key:"J-IV",   pos:[6,7],   len:2, label:"Wrapping Material",             table:"J-IV",   ref:"J.4.6" },
    { key:"J-V",    pos:[8,9],   len:2, label:"Cushioning &amp; Dunnage",      table:"J-V",    ref:"J.4.7" },
    { key:"J-VI",   pos:[10,10], len:1, label:"Cushioning Thickness",          table:"J-VI",   ref:"J.4.8" },
    { key:"J-VII",  pos:[11,12], len:2, label:"Unit Container",                table:"J-VII",  ref:"J.4.9" },
    { key:"J-VIIb", pos:[13,14], len:2, label:"Intermediate Container",        table:"J-VII",  ref:"J.4.12" },
    { key:"J-VIII", pos:[15,15], len:1, label:"Unit Container Level",          table:"J-VIII", ref:"J.4.10" },
    { key:"J-X",    pos:[16,17], len:2, label:"Special Marking",               table:"J-X",    ref:"J.4.14" },
    { key:"J-IX",   pos:[18,18], len:1, label:"Level A Packing",               table:"J-IX",   ref:"J.4.13" },
    { key:"J-IXa",  pos:[19,19], len:1, label:"Level B Packing",               table:"J-IXa",  ref:"J.4.13" },
    { key:"J-IXb",  pos:[20,20], len:1, label:"Minimal Packing",               table:"J-IXb",  ref:"J.4.13" }
  ],

  /* Standalone tables not part of the 20-character sequence */
  extraFields: [
    { key:"J-VIIIa", label:"Optional Procedure Indicator", table:"J-VIIIa", ref:"J.4.10" }
  ],

  tables: {

  "J-I": {
    title:"Table J-I — Methods of preservation codes",
    note:"Codes 30, 40 and 50 are the family headings; the two-digit codes beneath each are the specific methods. Detail text is from section 5.2.3 of the standard.",
    rows:[
    ["10","Physical protection",
     "The unpreserved item is protected from physical damage and mechanical malfunction. Cushioning, dunnage, blocking and bracing are applied as required to protect the item and the enclosing media and to restrict movement of the item within the container. All blocking and bracing, and its design and application, must be compatible with the item and its bearing load limitations. Materials are to be as clean and dry as practicable."],
    ["20","Preservative coating",
     "The item is treated with the appropriate preservative, then wrapped in material conforming to MIL-PRF-121 or QQ-A-1876. Flexible wraps snugly enclose the coated item and are secured to prevent unintentional unwrapping. Items coated with hard film preservative conforming to MIL-PRF-16173, Grade 1 or 4 may be exempted from wrapping once dried. Projections, sharp edges or other features that could damage the wrap are cushioned as required."],
    ["30","Waterproof protection (family heading)",
     "Basic group. The item is heat sealed within a waterproof or waterproof-greaseproof bag, with preservative applied as required. Projections, sharp edges or other physical characteristics that could damage the barrier are cushioned, and the item is also cushioned as required to mitigate shock and vibration."],
    ["31","Waterproof bag, heat sealed",
     "The preserved, wrapped and cushioned item is enclosed in a heat-sealed bag conforming to MIL-DTL-117, Type III, Class B, Style 2. When the contract or order calls for a carton or box to effect the unit container, the primary cushioning is placed between the outside of the bag and the inside of the carton or box."],
    ["32","Container, waterproof bag, heat sealed",
     "The preserved, wrapped and cushioned item is enclosed in a close fitting container (box) selected from table C-I, which in turn is enclosed in a heat-sealed waterproof bag conforming to MIL-DTL-117, Type III, Class B, Style 2."],
    ["33","Greaseproof-waterproof bag, heat sealed",
     "The preserved, wrapped and cushioned item is enclosed in a close fitting heat-sealed bag conforming to MIL-DTL-117, Type II, Class C, Style 1, 2 or 3. When the contract or order calls for a carton or box to effect the unit container, the primary cushioning is placed between the outside of the bag and the inside of the carton or box."],
    ["40","Watervaporproof protection (family heading)",
     "Basic group. The item is heat sealed within a watervaporproof enclosure, with preservative applied as required. Projections, sharp edges or other physical characteristics that could damage the enclosure are cushioned, and the item is also cushioned as required to mitigate shock and vibration."],
    ["41","Watervaporproof bag, heat sealed",
     "The preserved, wrapped and cushioned item is enclosed in a close fitting heat-sealed bag conforming to one of: MIL-DTL-117, Type I, Class E, Style 1, 2 or 3; MIL-DTL-117, Type I, Class F, Style 1 (ESD sensitive items only); MIL-DTL-117, Type II, Class E, Style 1; or MIL-DTL-117, Type IV, Class E, Style 1. Where Type II, Class E, Style 1 bags are selected they are limited to the restrictions detailed in MIL-PRF-131 for Class 2 material."],
    ["42","Container, watervaporproof bag, heat sealed, container",
     "The preserved, wrapped and cushioned item is enclosed in a close fitting inner container (box) selected from table C-I, then enclosed in a heat-sealed bag conforming to MIL-DTL-117, Type I, Class E, Style 1 or Type II, Class E, Style 1. Bags conforming to MIL-DTL-6060 are used when the construction limitations of MIL-DTL-117 are exceeded. The sealed bag is then enclosed within an appropriate outer container (box) selected from table C-II."],
    ["43","Floating watervaporproof bag, heat sealed",
     "The preserved, wrapped and cushioned item, anchored or shock mounted as necessary, is enclosed in a heat-sealed bag conforming to MIL-DTL-6060."],
    ["44","Rigid container (other than metal), sealed",
     "The preserved, wrapped and cushioned item is enclosed in a sealed, snug fitting rigid container other than all metal. Any such container may be used provided the sealed container gives a water vapor transmission rate not exceeding 0.075 gram per 100 square inches per 24 hours when tested in accordance with ASTM D4279."],
    ["45","Rigid metal container, sealed",
     "The preserved, wrapped and cushioned item is snugly enclosed in a sealed rigid metal container. Any type of rigid metal container with a machine seamed or gasketed closure may be used. The container is vacuum sealed when specified in the contract or purchase order, or when dictated by the requirements of the item."],
    ["50","Watervaporproof protection with desiccant (family heading)",
     "Basic group. The item is heat sealed in a watervaporproof enclosure with activated desiccant, and every unit pack in this group also includes a humidity indicator. Desiccant conforms to MIL-D-3464, Type I unless Type II or III is specified, in standard unit sized bags, strategically placed so it is not load bearing and never in direct contact with critical surfaces of the item. Quantity is computed by Formula I or II. Humidity indicators conform to MS20003, secured directly behind the inspection window or immediately within the closure seal; externally mounted indicators conform to SAE AS26860. Where bags are used they are sized with enough surface area to permit two subsequent resealings after item inspection."],
    ["51","Watervaporproof bag, heat sealed, with desiccant",
     "The preserved, wrapped, cushioned and desiccated item, with humidity indicator, is enclosed in a heat-sealed bag conforming to one of: MIL-DTL-117, Type I, Class E, Style 1, 2 or 3; MIL-DTL-117, Type II, Class E, Style 1; or MIL-DTL-117, Type IV, Class E, Style 1. Where Type II, Class E, Style 1 bags are selected they are limited to the restrictions detailed in MIL-PRF-131 for Class 2 material."],
    ["52","Container, watervaporproof bag, heat sealed, container, with desiccant",
     "The preserved, wrapped, cushioned and desiccated item, with humidity indicator, is enclosed in a close fitting inner container (box) selected from table C-I, then enclosed in a heat-sealed bag conforming to MIL-DTL-117, Type I, Class E, Style 1; Type II, Class E, Style 1; or Type IV, Class E, Style 1. Bags conforming to MIL-DTL-6060 are used when the construction limitations of MIL-DTL-117 are exceeded. The sealed bag is then enclosed within an appropriate outer container (box) selected from table C-II."],
    ["53","Floating watervaporproof bag, heat sealed, with desiccant",
     "The preserved, wrapped, cushioned and desiccated item, with humidity indicator, anchored or shock mounted as necessary, is enclosed in a sealed bag conforming to MIL-DTL-6060. When specified, a window of MIL-PRF-22191, Type I material is provided in the bag for packs of 15 cubic feet or larger, and externally mounted plug type humidity indicators conforming to SAE AS26860 are used. Where an exterior container is placed over the floating bag, a removable inspection port is provided to coincide with the inspection window or humidity plug."],
    ["54","Rigid container (other than metal), sealed, with desiccant",
     "The preserved, wrapped, cushioned and desiccated item, with humidity indicator, is enclosed in a sealed, close fitting rigid container other than all metal. Any such container may be used provided it gives a water vapor transmission rate not exceeding 0.075 gram per 100 square inches per 24 hours when tested in accordance with ASTM D4279 using the constant atmosphere method."],
    ["55","Rigid metal container, sealed, with desiccant",
     "The preserved, wrapped, cushioned and desiccated item, with humidity indicator, is enclosed in a sealed, close fitting metal container. Any type of rigid metal container with a machine seamed or welded closure, or a reusable container with a gasketed or threaded closure, is used."],
    ["ZZ","See J.4.1.b",
     "Supplementary or special requirements apply which are not represented by the code symbols. Details of the requirement must be provided with the acquisition document."]
  ]},

  "J-Ia": {
    title:"Table J-Ia — Specialized preservation codes",
    note:"Specialized preservation codes are typically all-inclusive for preserving an item. All requirement-code digits after the method of preservation enhance the 1st and 2nd digits.",
    rows:[
    ["AE","Seal or plug all openings and preserve by Method 10."],
    ["AH","Preserve Method 20 as follows: Fog spray or flush internally with preservative indicated by preservation code. All openings shall then be plugged or sealed to prevent entrance of dirt and moisture. Exterior unpainted ferrous metal surfaces shall be coated with a suitable paint or enamel, or coated with cold application, nontacky, corrosion preventive compound conforming to MIL-PRF-16173, Grade 4."],
    ["AU","Preservative compounds shall not be applied to windings, commutators or peripheries of armatures or rotors. Shafts shall be coated with MIL-PRF-16173, Grade 2 preservative and wrapped with MIL-PRF-121 material, secured in place with ASTM D5486 tape. Commutators shall be wrapped with MIL-PRF-121 material, held in place with ASTM D5486 tape. Exposed surfaces of steel collector rings shall be coated with MIL-PRF-16173, Grade 2 preservative. No preservative is required for bronze, brass or corrosion resisting metals. All collector rings shall be wrapped with MIL-PRF-121 material, secured in place with ASTM D5486 tape. Corrodible surfaces, except shafts, commutators, and collector rings, may be preserved by the use of insulating varnish applied during the manufacturing process. In addition to the foregoing requirements, armatures and rotors shall be wrapped with MIL-PRF-121 material, secured with ASTM D5486 tape."],
    ["AW","Preserve in accordance with any of the following alternate methods (used for gaskets and similar items): (a) Seal in bags conforming to Class B, C or E of MIL-DTL-117, using stiffening material internally if needed to maintain rigidity. (b) Preservation method 42 or 44. (c) Place between sheet of, or in fold of, corrugated fiberboard of sufficient stiffness to resist bending, overwrap with waterproof wrapping paper conforming to PPP-B-1055 and seal with pressure sensitive tape conforming to ASTM D5486 or adhesive conforming to MMM-A-260. Authorization to use other waterproof barrier materials may be granted upon request."],
    ["BC","Preserve by Method 20 as follows: Coat all pieces of set with preservative compound conforming to MIL-PRF-16173, Grade 4. Wrap or bag each preserved piece individually in MIL-PRF-121 material. Cushion or segregate individually wrapped or bagged pieces in the storage container to prevent movement and possible physical damage. (Segregated identical pieces, such as buckets and seal strips, are to be kept as close together in the container as possible to facilitate ease of counting.) Individually preserved, wrapped or bagged pieces need not be identified since container markings are in accordance with MIL-STD-129. Itemized packing lists for inclusion within or attachment to the outside of the container shall be furnished in accordance with MIL-STD-129. The lists shall show quantity and nomenclature of all items included in the set. (Used for turbine blade sets and similar items.)"],
    ["BD","Remove parts made of rubber, fiber, or nonmetallic materials adversely affected by preservative compounds and package by Method 41 without a preservative. Preserve metal parts of assembly to conform to the requirements of Method 40. Mark the bag containing nonmetallic parts “Parts for Assembly” and include it within, or securely attached to, the pack containing metal parts in a manner which will assure its being found when the pack is opened. (Use for couplings and similar items.)"],
    ["BL","Plug or seal all openings and preserve using Method 20."],
    ["DB","Preserve by Method 10 modified as follows: Preserve in transparent barrier bag made of A-A-3174 or Type III MIL-PRF-22191 material. A-A-3174 or MIL-PRF-22191, Type III material, A-A-3129 or PPP-C-795 cushioning shall be used to cushion sharp edges and protrusions of the preserved items. Bag closure shall be made by any suitable means, except that staples shall not be used. When use of a bag is not practicable, the item shall be completely wrapped in the above barrier or cushioning material and secured with pressure sensitive tape. Also, the use of shaped or molded packs utilizing MIL-PRF-22191 or A-A-3174 materials in conjunction with plastic coated board is acceptable provided the pack’s cube is not increased and the pack meets the tests specified in Appendix G. Strip or block form of multiple packages shall incorporate provisions for separating unit quantities."],
    ["DC","Preserve by Method 20 modified as follows: Preserve in a transparent barrier wrap made of Type II, MIL-PRF-22191 barrier material, or bag conforming to Type II, Class C, Style 2 of MIL-DTL-117. MIL-PRF-22191, Type II barrier material shall be used to cushion sharp edges and protrusions of item to prevent bag puncture. A-A-3129 or PPP-C-795 may also be used to cushion sharp edges and protrusions if item is first wrapped in MIL-PRF-22191, Type II barrier material. The bag closure shall be made by any suitable means, except that staples shall not be used. Also, the use of shaped, preformed or molded packages utilizing MIL-PRF-22191 or A-A-3174 materials in conjunction with plastic coated board is acceptable, provided that the package cube is not increased and materials are compatible with preservative specified. However, these packages shall be capable of meeting the tests specified in Appendix G. Strip or block form of multiple packages shall incorporate provisions for separating unit quantities."],
    ["DR","Preserve by Method 30 as follows: Each unit shall have all internal fluid-carrying passages, which are not prelubricated, filled with the specified preservative, allowing space for internal thermal expansion. If filling is not practical, the unit shall be internally fog-sprayed or flushed, then drained to the drip point. All ports, fittings, openings, etc., shall be capped or plugged with noncorrosive (non-interacting) metal caps or plugs conforming to NAS 847 or equivalent. All hydraulic preservative operating fluid used shall be filtered through a 3 micron absolute filter prior to being used as specified above. Exterior bare metal surfaces, subject to corrosion, shall be coated with compound conforming to MIL-PRF-16173, Grade 2 or MIL-C-11796, Class 3. Unit shall be wrapped with a greaseproof wrap conforming to MIL-PRF-121 or equivalent; seal seams with ASTM D5486 tape to effect a measure of waterproofness and prevent unwrapping. The unit must be adequately cushioned with material specified and placed in a grade V3c container fabricated in accordance with ASTM D5118/D5118M (as a minimum), Style FOL or CSSC. All seams, corners, and manufacturer’s joint shall be tape-sealed with two inch tape conforming to ASTM D5486, Type III or IV."],
    ["DW","Preserve by Method 52 as follows: Item shall be cleaned, wrapped, blocked and braced, with desiccant in an interior fiberboard box fabricated in accordance with ASTM D5118/D5118M, Class domestic. Desiccant shall be placed inside the fiberboard box. A humidity indicator shall be placed on the outside of the fiberboard box. MIL-PRF-131 barrier material, sealed as required, shall be utilized around the first container. The cushioning, to be specified under the cushioning code and in the thickness required to adequately protect the item, shall be placed between the barrier and the outer container."],
    ["EK","Preserve by Method 10 as follows: Each bolt shall have the shank and threads protected by means of a sleeve extending over the full length of the shank and thread. The sleeve shall be manufactured from paperboard, asphalt impregnated chipboard, or spiral wrap of kraft paper over chipboard, lined with material conforming to MIL-PRF-121. Plastic sleeve coverings may also be used."],
    ["GS","Preserve by Method 33 (modified) in a transparent, flexible, sealable, volatile corrosion inhibitor treated bag conforming to MIL-DTL-22020. The interleaf furnished inside each Class 2, cold sealable bag shall be withdrawn after inserting item and prior to final sealing in accordance with MIL-DTL-22020. Items with sharp edges or protrusions shall be wrapped with sufficient layers of transparent, flexible, pressure (cold) sealable volatile corrosion inhibitor barrier material conforming to MIL-PRF-22019, Type II to prevent bag puncture. The latex coated (nonprinted) side of the barrier material shall always be facing the item. Alternately, the item may be completely wrapped with transparent, flexible, pressure (cold) sealable volatile corrosion inhibitor barrier material conforming to MIL-PRF-22019, Type II as indicated above and further preserved in a transparent barrier bag conforming to Type II, Class C, Style 2 of MIL-DTL-117. Closure shall be by heat-sealing when this alternate method is used. In addition to markings required elsewhere in the contract, unit identification and caution labels shall be in accordance with MIL-STD-129."],
    ["GX","Preserve by Method 41 using an approved ESD control program (see 5.2.4.1.1) as follows: Items subject to damage by electromagnetic and electrostatic field forces shall be initially wrapped in material conforming to MIL-PRF-81705, Type III, or bags conforming to MIL-DTL-117, Type II, Class H, Style 2, and sufficiently cushioned in material conforming to A-A-3129, Type I, Grade B or PPP-C-795, Class 2 or MIL-DTL-81997, Type II or PPP-C-1797, Type II or A-A-59136, Class 1, Grade B or MIL-PRF-26514, Type III, Class 2, to protect item and to prevent bag puncture, and unit packed in a heat-sealed bag conforming to MIL-DTL-117, Type I, Class F, Style 1. Alternately if applicable, reclosable cushioned pouches conforming to MIL-DTL-81997, Type I may be used in lieu of initial wrap and cushioning. Lead or terminal configurations for all items shall be maintained as manufactured without causing loads or stresses capable of causing damage to the item. Materials used to maintain item position and lead or terminal configuration shall permit item removal without damage to the item. Electrostatic discharge (ESD) sensitive caution labels shall be applied in accordance with MIL-STD-129."],
    ["HM","Packaging and marking for hazardous materials shall comply with applicable requirements for Performance Oriented Packaging contained in the International Air Transport Association (IATA) Dangerous Goods Regulations or the International Maritime Dangerous Goods Code (IMDG) and with Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) Title 29, Title 40 and Title 49. All performance test requirements shall be supported by certificates and reports attesting to the date and the results obtained from performance oriented packaging testing. The contractor, if not a self-certifier, shall be responsible for assuring that third party sources providing performance testing services are, in fact, registered with the Department of Transportation. The contractor’s signed certification that the packaged configuration meets IATA or IMDG requirements shall be incorporated on the DD Form 250, Material Inspection and Receiving Report, and other related acceptance document if the DD Form 250 is not used. All certificates and reports shall be available for inspection by authorized Government representatives for a period of three years."],
    ["JF","Preserve by Method 10 — Items shall be preserved in a vacuum formed skin pack, formed from either cellulose acetate, cellulose butyrate or cellulose propionate. The material shall be 10 to 15 mils minimum thickness prior to draw and 2 to 4 mils thickness after draw. Class domestic fiberboard meeting the requirements of ASTM D4727/D4727M shall be used as a stiffener."]
  ]},

